## Learning Goals

By the end of the course, I aim to be able to:

- Apply signal transformations and filtering methods to scientific data.
- Model and analyze stochastic noise using probability theory and power spectral densities.
- Implement statistical detection and parameter-estimation techniques.
- Solve computational optimization problems using particle swarm optimization.
- Apply introductory machine-learning methods to astronomical data-analysis problems.
- Use Git and GitHub to maintain a clear, reproducible record of code development.

